    desc: "Cross-platform mobile app that converts songs into precisely-timed haptic patterns — making music physically feelable for deaf and hard-of-hearing users or anyone. The core engineering challenge was scheduler drift: setInterval accumulates 100–200ms of timing error over a 60-second song, making beats feel broken. Solved with a look-ahead scheduler based on the Web Audio scheduling pattern — a 30ms interval pre-schedules events via setTimeout with wall-clock offsets, bounding worst-case jitter to ~30ms (well below the 80ms human rhythmic perception threshold). A dual-platform HapticEngine dispatches iOS Taptic Engine styles (5 intensity levels: Soft → Heavy) and Android Vibration API duration patterns independently. Surface Mode fires double-knock sequences that excite hard surface resonance — physically audible through glass and wood — extending the use case from personal handheld to shared ambient experience.",
